2. Third-party code that is NOT included (cloned at pinned commits by scripts/procgen/setup_external.py)

   - JacobPfau/procgenAISC (MIT)
   - KarolisRam/colour-shape-goal-misgeneralization (MIT) and its procgenAISC submodule (MIT)
   - jbkjr/train-procgen-pytorch (Langosco et al.; fork of joonleesky/train-procgen-pytorch) -- no license file
   - KarolisRam/train-procgen (submodule of the colour-shape repository) -- no license file
   The two train-procgen repositories carry no license, so they are not redistributed here.
   The Attribute Maze trainers in src/gm_geometry/training/colour_shape/ and
   scripts/procgen/arch/ call into, and follow the structure of, these trainers (argument parsing,
   environment and logger construction, PPO agent setup) and reimplement the IMPALA network with
   the same parameter names so that the trained checkpoints load.

